{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice","id":1524841,"title":"M20 different High Ritual practice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-31T14:43:03-07:00","id":1524841,"title":"M20 different High Ritual practice","content":"When people talk about the High Ritual practice, we always imagine hermetics HR, involving pentagrams, celestial bodies, symbols, enochian, etc. But the entry in M20 talks about several forms of high ritual.<br /> <br /> So, how would be HR if used by a mage (or technomacer) that has as paradigm, science (sleeper or awakened)? Would the rituals be the long hour of work and study on the fields of science related to the individual paradigm?<br /> What would be the &quot;complexity&quot; and &quot;details&quot; that HR often have, in the case of a paradigm like that?<br /> <br /> Would like to read some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T15:13:03-07:00","id":1524843,"title":"","content":"In the printed material there is a Heremetic study group called &quot;<b>High Saturday</b>.&quot; It embraces Afro-Caribbean ritualism. There have been Heremetics in the printed material that used Vedic/Indian ritualism and another that embraced Norse ritualism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-31-2023, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T17:58:19-07:00","id":1524854,"title":"","content":"It helps to remember that Rituals are there to provide support for a spell, but are not the spell itself. Casting an impromptu spell is dancing without music, Rituals are music made specifically for that dance.<br /> Writing down formulas or reciting Ohm's law gets you in the mindset for that spell? Go for it! Recreating a symbolic chemical reaction to enchant a potion or compiling software libraries for your magi-hack, the specifics themselves don't matter that much as long as they guide you into what the spell is supposed to do. As such, Rituals will often symbolically re-enact the spell effect in an abstracted manner. Your Technomancer wants to bring down an ISP switch? One might end the ritual with ramming a screwdriver through a network card, another might put hours into writing a 'virus' that gets the job done.<br /> <br /> Complexity and details are the things that arise from making the Ritual more effective in aiding the spell. One big thing there is sympathetic connection, ie something that connects the target with the spell. In my above example, giving the network card the screwdriver might be a lot more efficient if the card has an active connection to the switch in question. Maybe extra efficient if you also find out the correct port, and know how the target hardware actually works. The more details you add (and the more insight you have about the processes involved) to get the target 'zeroed in', the more complex your Rituals gets.<br /> A while ago there was some hubbub about a witch coven that published a binding spell designed to target the then-president of the US, using a carrot as sympathetic connector. Which I would rule as a very low-tier component for the job, but it gets the idea across even to laymen.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Technomancy or other quasi-scientific paradigms actually lend themselves rather well to the hermetic style if you swap out traditional components with some that are closer to more 'modern' equivalents. Instead of a circle, draw a circuit diagram on the floor, representing something that aligns with what the spell should do. Burn electrolyte and soldering wire instead of incense. That kind of thing. I personally treat these reskins as just flavor, but it might be sufficient depending on how involved you want to get with your Ritual construction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T01:04:53-07:00","id":1524864,"title":"","content":"High Ritual Magick is typified by its focus (no pun intended) on complexity and theatrics. Every ritual is a production. Each element in its right place, the mage engaging with great mastery and showmanship.<br /> <br /> My vision of a technomancer High Ritual Magician is an Etherite mad scientist going full &quot;Doctor Frankenstein flipping the switch during a thunderstorm&quot; routine. Their lab filled with strange devices; tesla coils, bubbling beakers, dripping alembics, wires and tubes everywhere, etc. The genius clad in white lab coat, goggles, and thick, oversized rubber gloves. Ranting about how &quot;They&quot; called them mad, and dramatically explaining their process (either to no one, or to one or more assistants who hang on the good doctor's every word). Shouting &quot;BEHOLD!&quot; and &quot;It's Alive! IT'S ALIVE!&quot;, while cackling madly. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/QRtN32Qjsgo?si=9S07THVhDOjsoFTI\" target=\"_blank\">Singing optional</a>. Flipping switches as lightning strikes.<br /> <br /> This isn't just Weird Science. It's High Ritual Science!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T02:21:25-07:00","id":1524867,"title":"","content":"That's a good one! Aside from being fun, it also illustrates that Ritual specifics depend on just how willing the caster is to accept overt magical effects. The closer you get to Enlightened Science paradigms, the less abstract and symbolic your Ritual components become. A reskin of hermetic procedure would not work, because to them it's humbug. At the far end of the spectrum you have Rituals that <i>almost </i>resemble a mundane procedure to achieve the effect you are going for, and the Magick just cheats a little to overcome functional gaps that prevent a Sleeper from doing the same thing.<br /> <br /> As an aside, there is a good chance that song and dance were the very first Ritual components employed. Just as a working chant supports physical labor, the same is true for casting a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T05:04:08-07:00","id":1524868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524854#post1524854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps to remember that Rituals are there to provide support for a spell, but are not the spell itself. Casting an impromptu spell is dancing without music, Rituals are music made specifically for that dance.<br /> Writing down formulas or reciting Ohm's law gets you in the mindset for that spell? Go for it! Recreating a symbolic chemical reaction to enchant a potion or compiling software libraries for your magi-hack, the specifics themselves don't matter that much as long as they guide you into what the spell is supposed to do. As such, Rituals will often symbolically re-enact the spell effect in an abstracted manner. Your Technomancer wants to bring down an ISP switch? One might end the ritual with ramming a screwdriver through a network card, another might put hours into writing a 'virus' that gets the job done.<br /> <br /> Complexity and details are the things that arise from making the Ritual more effective in aiding the spell. One big thing there is sympathetic connection, ie something that connects the target with the spell. In my above example, giving the network card the screwdriver might be a lot more efficient if the card has an active connection to the switch in question. Maybe extra efficient if you also find out the correct port, and know how the target hardware actually works. The more details you add (and the more insight you have about the processes involved) to get the target 'zeroed in', the more complex your Rituals gets.<br /> A while ago there was some hubbub about a witch coven that published a binding spell designed to target the then-president of the US, using a carrot as sympathetic connector. Which I would rule as a very low-tier component for the job, but it gets the idea across even to laymen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is exactly the kind of answer I was looking for. Thank you very much. Especially the part of the downtime representation of the practice and the complexity/detail thing. Indeed, science can be one big complex and detailed bitch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524854#post1524854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, Technomancy or other quasi-scientific paradigms actually lend themselves rather well to the hermetic style if you swap out traditional components with some that are closer to more 'modern' equivalents. Instead of a circle, draw a circuit diagram on the floor, representing something that aligns with what the spell should do. Burn electrolyte and soldering wire instead of incense. That kind of thing. I personally treat these reskins as just flavor, but it might be sufficient depending on how involved you want to get with your Ritual construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I tend to think that all hermetic HR is the same, but I would say that no two hermetics use HR the same way. Of course, they might share some common theories, but there should be an immense diversity of HR beliefs.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I wonder which houses would be more prone to have members that have a quasi-scientific paradigm. Of course House Thig is on this list (which is now House Verditius, but I guess the merge brought Thig paradigm into it). House Flambeau is known to recruit physicists and scientist when their fields involves elements or forces of destruction. I could see a bani Tytalus with such a paradigm too, maybe...<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524864#post1524864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Ritual Magick is typified by its focus (no pun intended) on complexity and theatrics. Every ritual is a production. Each element in its right place, the mage engaging with great mastery and showmanship.<br /> <br /> My vision of a technomancer High Ritual Magician is an Etherite mad scientist going full &quot;Doctor Frankenstein flipping the switch during a thunderstorm&quot; routine. Their lab filled with strange devices; tesla coils, bubbling beakers, dripping alembics, wires and tubes everywhere, etc. The genius clad in white lab coat, goggles, and thick, oversized rubber gloves. Ranting about how &quot;They&quot; called them mad, and dramatically explaining their process (either to no one, or to one or more assistants who hang on the good doctor's every word). Shouting &quot;BEHOLD!&quot; and &quot;It's Alive! IT'S ALIVE!&quot;, while cackling madly. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/QRtN32Qjsgo?si=9S07THVhDOjsoFTI\" target=\"_blank\">Singing optional</a>. Flipping switches as lightning strikes.<br /> <br /> This isn't just Weird Science. It's High Ritual Science!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I don't think that theatrics is something necessary and intrinsic to HR, I can see it often being part of it, sure. But not in an intentional way. HR is complex and their users should be very serious about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T11:45:39-07:00","id":1524873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524868#post1524868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't think that theatrics is something necessary and intrinsic to HR, I can see it often being part of it, sure. But not in an intentional way. HR is complex and their users should be very serious about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many kinds of theatrics. The one outlined above is obviously of the campy, b-movie variety.<br /> <br /> But go to a theater putting on a production of Shakespeare and tell me the performers aren't taking their roles seriously. (I mean, I guess it depends a lot on the troupe. But there are very professional actors who hold the whole process as Serious Business. Even as they're delivering 17th century innuendo and &quot;yo momma&quot; jokes.)<br /> <br /> Moreover, the process of High Ritual Magick doesn't require &quot;theatrical&quot; performance in the mundane sense. Steps must be followed. The space must be decorated with the proper paraphernalia. The magician(s) must often dress up in uniform, and possibly bathe and fast before they begin.<br /> <br /> What separates High Ritual from &quot;normal&quot; ritual is the dedication to forms. It is all, in the caster's mind, necessary for the process. Both for its symbolic (or &quot;scientific&quot;) significance, and because of the sense of gravitas and import being placed on it. Bringing the participant(s) to such a height of emotional intensity, the part of the mind that dwells in &quot;magical thinking&quot; cannot hope but accept that the working WILL succeed. It HAS TO.<br /> <br /> (In the Real World, this is the kind of emotional intensity that convinces people their spells work. In Mage: The Ascension, it allows them to channel the force of Will needed to bend Reality to their designs. The High Ritual Magick user simply makes this kind of convention their standard operating procedure.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T12:46:22-07:00","id":1524879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524873#post1524873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What separates High Ritual from &quot;normal&quot; ritual is the dedication to forms. It is all, in the caster's mind, necessary for the process. Both for its symbolic (or &quot;scientific&quot;) significance, and because of the sense of gravitas and import being placed on it. Bringing the participant(s) to such a height of emotional intensity, the part of the mind that dwells in &quot;magical thinking&quot; cannot hope but accept that the working WILL succeed. It HAS TO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. Being in the right mindset is an important part of the procedure, too: The robes (or labcoat), the ceremony (or protocol), all the theatrics are there to clearly separate the mundane from the Magick (or SCIENCE\u2122\u200b). It's the same as people keeping their work spaces separate from their living spaces. Or, like a boxer getting a pep talk before going into a match.<br /> Even the most down to earth Verbena wouldn't use their athame to cut tomatoes, unless it's a cooking spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524868#post1524868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having said that, I wonder which houses would be more prone to have members that have a quasi-scientific paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally a fan of House Skopos, who are looking for overlaps between Magick and quantum reality. Tiny House with only a handful of members, but fascinating concept.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T13:14:17-07:00","id":1524880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524873#post1524873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are many kinds of theatrics. The one outlined above is obviously of the campy, b-movie variety.<br /> <br /> But go to a theater putting on a production of Shakespeare and tell me the performers aren't taking their roles seriously. (I mean, I guess it depends a lot on the troupe. But there are very professional actors who hold the whole process as Serious Business. Even as they're delivering 17th century innuendo and &quot;yo momma&quot; jokes.)<br /> <br /> Moreover, the process of High Ritual Magick doesn't require &quot;theatrical&quot; performance in the mundane sense. Steps must be followed. The space must be decorated with the proper paraphernalia. The magician(s) must often dress up in uniform, and possibly bathe and fast before they begin.<br /> <br /> What separates High Ritual from &quot;normal&quot; ritual is the dedication to forms. It is all, in the caster's mind, necessary for the process. Both for its symbolic (or &quot;scientific&quot;) significance, and because of the sense of gravitas and import being placed on it. Bringing the participant(s) to such a height of emotional intensity, the part of the mind that dwells in &quot;magical thinking&quot; cannot hope but accept that the working WILL succeed. It HAS TO.<br /> <br /> (In the Real World, this is the kind of emotional intensity that convinces people their spells work. In Mage: The Ascension, it allows them to channel the force of Will needed to bend Reality to their designs. The High Ritual Magick user simply makes this kind of convention their standard operating procedure.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I thoughr you were saying the mage himself would be &quot;acting&quot; (instead of &quot;being&quot;) in a sense that it doesn't really believes in that.<br /> <br /> Since you don't mean that, I agree.<br /> I just disagree when you say that the scenario must be prepared, that he must dress differently, etc. A ritual doesn't need to have a scenario nor dressing code or anything specific. It could be the mage doing mental calculations and revising laws and theories in his head. Maybe putting it on paper or somethinf like that. Of course, it must be a ritual, something kind of complex that has lots of details.<br /> <br /> Now, if you were talking in a generic way and only giving examples, then we agree again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524879#post1524879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm personally a fan of House Skopos, who are looking for overlaps between Magick and quantum reality. Tiny House with only a handful of members, but fascinating concept.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I think this one could enter the list too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T14:30:29-07:00","id":1524885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524879#post1524879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the most down to earth Verbena wouldn't use their athame to cut tomatoes, unless it's a cooking spell.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The Verbana, being rural peasant magicians, absolutely would use their household items in High Ritual.<br /> <br /> Granted, some might not. Some might very well keep precious ritual athames and other items in special boxes, only used on special occasions.<br /> <br /> But many others wouldn't. Witchcraft is all about using the materials you have on hand. The same broomstick you fly in on is used to sweep up afterwards. The ritual dagger used to cut the world into shape is used to cut the tomatoes for dinner. If anything, some Verbana might consider its duel-use a benefit, as they're symbolically interweaving their magical and mundane lives together. They don't establish any kind of artificial distinction between the two, because the world itself is suffused with magic.<br /> <br /> (Granted, some Verbana who set up their High Ritual Magick would at least <i>wash</i> and anoint their athame with oils/herbs before using it. Here in the coven, we still have <i>standards</i>.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T15:44:45-07:00","id":1524889,"title":"","content":"Household items, because of their homeiness, are emotionally charged. The tools people made their livings with, many made by their own hands, would be profoundly significant. So, yes Verbena witches and those in similar circumstances would find profound power there. <br /> <br /> Hermetics would have to seek other ways to make their tools profound. But there are many paths to High Ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T05:45:11-07:00","id":1524909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524885#post1524885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. The Verbana, being rural peasant magicians, absolutely would use their household items in High Ritual.<br /> <br /> Granted, some might not. Some might very well keep precious ritual athames and other items in special boxes, only used on special occasions.<br /> <br /> But many others wouldn't. Witchcraft is all about using the materials you have on hand. The same broomstick you fly in on is used to sweep up afterwards. The ritual dagger used to cut the world into shape is used to cut the tomatoes for dinner. If anything, some Verbana might consider its duel-use a benefit, as they're symbolically interweaving their magical and mundane lives together. They don't establish any kind of artificial distinction between the two, because the world itself is suffused with magic.<br /> <br /> (Granted, some Verbana who set up their High Ritual Magick would at least <i>wash</i> and anoint their athame with oils/herbs before using it. Here in the coven, we still have <i>standards</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, and I concede the tomatoes.<br /> <br /> I was about to draw a line at using it to clean finger nails, but then remembered seeing literal nail dirt used as a ritual component before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T06:13:56-07:00","id":1524910,"title":"","content":"It comes to mind the idea that a High Ritual VA &quot;computer wizard&quot; would be one of those that would rap a lot about the &quot;elegance of the code&quot;, following and improving uppon paradigms and protocols. And would be very offended if someone would call what they do &quot;a hack&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T09:15:44-07:00","id":1524924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524910#post1524910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It comes to mind the idea that a High Ritual VA &quot;computer wizard&quot; would be one of those that would rap a lot about the &quot;elegance of the code&quot;, following and improving uppon paradigms and protocols. And would be very offended if someone would call what they do &quot;a hack&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what would be the difference between High Ritual &quot;computer wizard&quot; and someone similar using the practice Reality Hacking...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T14:19:57-07:00","id":1524933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524924#post1524924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what would be the difference between High Ritual &quot;computer wizard&quot; and someone similar using the practice Reality Hacking...</div> </div> </div> </div>The beauty of M20 is you don't need to choose. A character can have up to three Practices. So you can have a Reality Hacker that also uses High Ritual Magick.<br /> <br /> To answer the question, though, a Reality Hacker who wasn't a High Ritual Magician might do a lot more &quot;code-bashing&quot;. It wouldn't matter if the code was perfect, only that it worked. Bugs can be ironed out in later versions. They still do all-night coding sessions and tinker with their hardware, because that's a part of Mage I like to call &quot;Upkeep&quot; (the activities needed to prepare one's Instruments and maintain one's ability to do Magick). But they don't make a big production out of it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a High Ritual Magick user might assemble all their best hardware, wired in sequence. Meticulously organize their tabs to make sure every program and resource is where they need it, when they need it. Thoroughly research beforehand, so they know exactly how the code is supposed to work prior to implementing it. Maybe start chugging energy drinks and blasting appropriate music, to ensure they're in the right headspace. Put on their VR headset, to get a constant feed of data without needing to look around to different monitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T04:58:05-07:00","id":1524970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524924#post1524924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what would be the difference between High Ritual &quot;computer wizard&quot; and someone similar using the practice Reality Hacking...</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be a common misunderstanding about what reality hacking is. Some people assume that it's \u201cthat reality as if it was a computer simulation\u201d, or something along those lines. It's not. Reality hacking is what Tony Stark did in the cave in the first Iron Man movie; what the Professor on Gilligan's Island was famous for doing; what McGyver did every week. It's also known as jury-rigging or kitbashing in its Coincidental applications: creative use of technology to achieve results outside of the design parameters. <br /> <br /> It's pretty much the <i>opposite</i> of High Ritual, which is all about being meticulous, making sure that you have the right tools for the job, and taking your time to get it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T06:22:18-07:00","id":1524971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524970#post1524970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be a common misunderstanding about what reality hacking is. Some people assume that it's \u201cthat reality as if it was a computer simulation\u201d, or something along those lines. It's not. Reality hacking is what Tony Stark did in the cave in the first Iron Man movie; what the Professor on Gilligan's Island was famous for doing; what McGyver did every week. It's also known as jury-rigging or kitbashing in its Coincidental applications: creative use of technology to achieve results outside of the design parameters.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the <i>opposite</i> of High Ritual, which is all about being meticulous, making sure that you have the right tools for the job, and taking your time to get it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Reality Hacking doesn't have to involve computers but it might do as well.<br /> Your description looks more alike to Gutter Magick than Reality Hacking. But practices (as instruments) often have an overlap.<br /> <br /> Now, the big question is: how would look like if you mix the practices that *seem* to be opposites, like High Ritual and Gutter Magick or Chaos Magick (I don't think Reality Hacking is the exact opposite of HR)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T08:37:15-07:00","id":1524977,"title":"","content":"Seems a bit odd trying to fuse these together (some kind of Practice hacking?), but.. for Chaos Magick the whole point is not having rules. I could see a Chaos Mage perform the most polished of High Rituals just to subvert expectations. Or alternatively, sprinkling bouts of deliberate anarchism and iconoclasm into the High Ritual just for the heightened contrast this would create.<br /> Edit: Or make it a <i>parody </i>of High Ritual and still have it working. Discordians seem especially fond of that one.<br /> <br /> Gutter Magick could simply take the 'excellence in execution' part of High Ritual while employing only 'low-tier' components, or vice versa. Again, I think that juxtaposition could be an interesting way to emphasize certain spell effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 11-03-2023, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T15:04:42-07:00","id":1524994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524971#post1524971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Reality Hacking doesn't have to involve computers but it might do as well.<br /> Your description looks more alike to Gutter Magick than Reality Hacking. But practices (as instruments) often have an overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed they do. In particular, Reality Hacking and Gutter Magick are both examples of Practices that put a lot of emphasis on improvising, of making it up as you go along. They're still distinct Practices; but they have a sort of kinship. <br /> <br /> Also: yes, computers can be involved in Reality Hacking; but the thing that sets Reality Hacking apart from computer hacking is that the focus (no pun intended) isn't on the computer in the former case: something else is being hacked; and if a computer is involved at all, its role is as component of what the mage is hacking rather than as the thing being hacked. A means to an end rather than the end itself. <br /> <br /> Also, the thing being hacked doesn't have to be a machine. One could hack, say, an election system. Not the digital voting booths (if there are any), but the <i>election process itself. </i>This would involve interacting with the process in some way \u2014 meddling in it, as it were \u2014 in order to take advantage of quirks within the system to get a result of your liking. That <i>could </i>be as straightforward as choosing who will win; or it could be less direct, like triggering (or suppressing) a riot. All that is needed for Reality Hacking to be invoked is a system with reasonably well defined rules and a means for the hacker to mess with those rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T01:34:44-07:00","id":1525015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524970#post1524970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be a common misunderstanding about what reality hacking is. Some people assume that it's \u201cthat reality as if it was a computer simulation\u201d, or something along those lines. It's not. Reality hacking is what Tony Stark did in the cave in the first Iron Man movie; what the Professor on Gilligan's Island was famous for doing; what McGyver did every week. It's also known as jury-rigging or kitbashing in its Coincidental applications: creative use of technology to achieve results outside of the design parameters.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the <i>opposite</i> of High Ritual, which is all about being meticulous, making sure that you have the right tools for the job, and taking your time to get it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. While there's certainly much differentiating the patient, perfection-minded science of High Ritual Magick and the creative process of Reality Hacking, I don't think these are necessarily incompatible.<br /> <br /> Under A Mechanistic Cosmos (and Everything is Data), Reality operates on rules. Input A -&gt; Output B. But, depending on the interpretation of the Paradigm, those rules are subject to change, or at least to being applied to novel forms. So long as you know the rules, you can bend or exploit them.<br /> <br /> A High Ritual Magician is, by necessity, imposing their Will on Reality, through both the strength of their conviction and the rigor of their preparations. No one said they were limited to only what rituals were made perfect in the time of Hermes Trismegistus (well, outside some members of the Order of Hermes). So long as your research was thorough and your preparations flawless, you can create new forms. Creativity is not the enemy of Perfection.<br /> <br /> You can have a Reality Hacker whose process is backed up by rigor and knowledge, and the will to impose themself on Reality. And you can have a High Ritual Magician who pushes the boundaries of what their Art &amp; Science allow. Indeed, both the Order of Hermes and the Order of Reason did exactly that, each in their turn.<br /> <br /> Bonisagus, the eponymous House founder and co-creator of the Order of Hermes, was a prolific hacker of Hermetic methods, and his House continues that tradition of elaborate Hermetic experimentation.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Order of Reason (and latterly the Technocratic Union) established a process of scientific rigor, yet revolutionized society on a technological, social, geographic, legal, religious, and even architectural level. They were hacking reality from the medieval into the modern, yet would insist they weren't being sloppy, lazy, or stupid in their processes. There's was no less High Ritual Science.<br /> <br /> It's unhelpful to say &quot;these two Practices are opposites and incompatible&quot;. One must instead ask &quot;how can these seemingly incompatible Practices intersect?&quot;<br /> <br /> (It helps to go back and read the descriptions of the Practices. As I did, when writing this comment.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T03:39:07-07:00","id":1525016,"title":"","content":"High Ritual is IMO kinda difficult to discuss because the write-up is essentially two different practices welded together. Like, the defining element of the practice is precision ritual and getting everything just right... but then the explanation is about that honing the mage's will. That secondary element doesn't necessarily follow from the first. Indeed, I suspect a lot of the examples it points towards wouldn't recognise that characterisation.<br /> <br /> For example, I could see a Chorister whose practice has that precision ritualism, but where their paradigm places the magic power outside themselves. They need to get everything just right, because that's what the entities giving them their power demand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T08:13:24-07:00","id":1525023,"title":"","content":"Part of it is that there's some mixing of what's Practice and what's Paradigm. High Ritual is a Practice; it wouldn't assume that it works by honing the Will, because <i>that's</i> Paradigm. Likewise, whole the Virtual Accepts (who are big on the Everything is Data Paradigm) are likely to explain Reality Hacking in Everything is Data terminology, Reality Hacking is a <i>Practice,</i> and not necessarily wedded to one Paradigm. That's where the Tony Stark reference comes in: Tony <i>isn't </i>a VA; if I had to place him in one of the existing factions, the closest fit would be the Syndicate. His Paradigm <i>isn't </i>\u201cEverything is Data\u201d, and I'm not even sure I'd call it a Mechanistic Universe. There <i>is </i>a large chunk of \u201cTechnology Holds All the Answers\u201d in his Paradigm; but that's about it. But what he does is very definitely Reality Hacking. <br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I never said that Reality Hacking and High Ritual are <i>incompatible; </i>that's just an assumption that you made from my comment about them lately being opposites. Nor did I say that High Ritual can't have Creativity, or that the Order of Hermes is stuck using a rigid system devised centuries ago. Again, you read that into it. <br /> <br /> The reason I say that the two are opposites is that High Ritual is all about preparation, whereas Reality Hacking is about adaptability. That's where their respective fortes are. The High Ritualist's creativity tends to manifest during the prep work, as he attempts to anticipate every eventuality; whereas the Reality Hacker's creativity tends to manifest in the moment, as he takes stock of what's available to him and evaluates how those tools might be used in unorthodox ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T07:57:13-08:00","id":1525163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1525023#post1525023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I say that the two are opposites is that High Ritual is all about preparation, whereas Reality Hacking is about adaptability. That's where their respective fortes are. The High Ritualist's creativity tends to manifest during the prep work, as he attempts to anticipate every eventuality; whereas the Reality Hacker's creativity tends to manifest in the moment, as he takes stock of what's available to him and evaluates how those tools might be used in unorthodox ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I would say that the practices, while kinda opposite, works very well together, because they complement each other. And the same can be said for Chaos magick and High Ritual. While HR is focused in preparations and details, when the shit hits the fan, Chaos Magick allows you to improvise and adapt, but still based on some of the prepararions and studies that are part of HR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T10:51:17-08:00","id":1525171,"title":"","content":"As long as they're both compatible with the same Paradigm, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T01:25:14-08:00","id":1525238,"title":"","content":"The thing is that what everybody here is describing is NOT Enlightened Science, but rather technomancy High Ritual.<br /> <br /> Real Enlightened Science High Ritual would involve meticulous calculations of EVERY single variable of the lab. It's not just about having a sterilized lab. You need to carefully study astronomy (no, not some silly thing like astrology, please! Totally disconnected things!) so that you can have a precise inference of the pattern of cosmic rays emittions, and thus adjust accordingly. Every single object inside the lab must be properly distributed, so that their electromagnetic fields do not interfere. Maybe 5 &quot;interferon devices&quot; have to be displaced in a pentagram circuitry in order to &quot;dissipate the electromagnetic fields caused the Earth's magma core&quot; (those silly superstitionists figured out by trial and error that pentagrams are the best forms of interferon dissipation, but they don't know &quot;Da Science&quot; of it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T01:29:49-08:00","id":1525239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524970#post1524970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be a common misunderstanding about what reality hacking is. Some people assume that it's \u201cthat reality as if it was a computer simulation\u201d, or something along those lines. It's not. Reality hacking is what Tony Stark did in the cave in the first Iron Man movie; what the Professor on Gilligan's Island was famous for doing; what McGyver did every week. It's also known as jury-rigging or kitbashing in its Coincidental applications: creative use of technology to achieve results outside of the design parameters.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the <i>opposite</i> of High Ritual, which is all about being meticulous, making sure that you have the right tools for the job, and taking your time to get it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't realize that Mages that can thus &quot;hack&quot; reality in this Neo (the character) Matrix style, are actually Marauders...<br /> <br /> &quot;It's all a computer simulation, reality ain't real, so I can just &quot;hack&quot; the &quot;code&quot; of the air to turn it into lead with my thoughts!&quot; - this is a sure way to cause Paradox NOT for lunatic himself, but for the closest unfortunate non delusional mage passing by...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 11-09-2023, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T01:43:23-08:00","id":1525240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1524977#post1524977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems a bit odd trying to fuse these together (some kind of Practice hacking?), but.. for Chaos Magick the whole point is not having rules. I could see a Chaos Mage perform the most polished of High Rituals just to subvert expectations. Or alternatively, sprinkling bouts of deliberate anarchism and iconoclasm into the High Ritual just for the heightened contrast this would create.<br /> Edit: Or make it a <i>parody </i>of High Ritual and still have it working. Discordians seem especially fond of that one.<br /> <br /> Gutter Magick could simply take the 'excellence in execution' part of High Ritual while employing only 'low-tier' components, or vice versa. Again, I think that juxtaposition could be an interesting way to emphasize certain spell effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have a &quot;Wizard's Circle&quot;, carefully drawn in detail over a large area with arcane geometric simbols... And inside you do Chaos Magic, where you then &quot;openly defy&quot; the &quot;imposed order&quot; of the outside area. For example, performing erratic dancing on the inside, sometimes leaving the boundaries of the &quot;containment area&quot; in order to &quot;disrupt orderly patterns&quot;.<br /> <br /> That could, in fact, be a potent form of Chaos Magic - let's call it &quot;defying chaos&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or it could be the other way around, it could be &quot;trying to impose order upon chaos&quot;. Imagine for instance a &quot;Tesla Coil&quot; that generates (seemingly) random bolts of electrical discharges. To toople it off, at the beginning of the ritual, you take your little Tesla devices and throw them up in the air, and let them land whatever they do. Then, on the outside circle, you meticulously dispose of all the devices you'll need to measure and &quot;redirect&quot; the outside electromagnetic fields. This could also be a VERY powerful form of HR study that tries to &quot;order the chaos&quot;.<br /> <br /> Both approaches are possible, with a distinct and opposite direction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T06:24:38-08:00","id":1525247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524841-m20-different-high-ritual-practice?p=1525238#post1525238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that what everybody here is describing is NOT Enlightened Science, but rather technomancy High Ritual.<br /> <br /> Real Enlightened Science High Ritual would involve meticulous calculations of EVERY single variable of the lab. It's not just about having a sterilized lab. You need to carefully study astronomy (no, not some silly thing like astrology, please! Totally disconnected things!) so that you can have a precise inference of the pattern of cosmic rays emittions, and thus adjust accordingly. Every single object inside the lab must be properly distributed, so that their electromagnetic fields do not interfere. Maybe 5 &quot;interferon devices&quot; have to be displaced in a pentagram circuitry in order to &quot;dissipate the electromagnetic fields caused the Earth's magma core&quot; (those silly superstitionists figured out by trial and error that pentagrams are the best forms of interferon dissipation, but they don't know &quot;Da Science&quot; of it)</div> </div> </div> </div>What we were describing would be someone with a scientific paradigm doing HR. This can include both technomancy (when symbolism are used) and Enlightened Science. I believe both would be pretty similar. <br /> <br /> Also, I believe that HR is more than objects and environment used. It's also about the mindset, the discipline and effort done in downtime. In the case of a scientific paradigm, that could be represented by the study of science and/or work and experiments. This is something that both Enlightened Science and technomancy would share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}